<div style="text-align: center">

# <span style="color: #e6a050">Auto Doors</span>

</div>
<div style="text-align: center">

*<span style="color: #e6a050">Approach : door opens. Leave : door closes. Simple as that.</span>*

</div>

<div style="text-align: center">

*The source code for all my Enshrouded mods is available on [**GitHub**](https://github.com/Fuzen777/Enshrouded-Mods) (MIT)*

</div>

Auto Doors is a **Kiln** mod. Inside a Flame Altar's area, doors opens when you, a survivor or your build camera comes near, and close once everyone has left.

It is a rebuild of the idea behind SellTheWorldGames' AutoDoors, with configurable distances and a mode for each door. It also doesn’t close your inventory/chest/craft menu if a door opens at the same time.

There is no on-screen prompt for any of this, so here is everything you can do.

---

## Controls

- **Shift + MMB** (controller: **LB + Y**) while looking at a door : look at a door and press it to change that door's mode. Each press moves to the next mode and a message tells you which one it is now.
- **Shift + F7**:  opens the Settings menu. (Same as Kiln settings, nicer to look at.)

Both keys can be changed in the **Keys** tab of Kiln's menu. Normally, it should only take away MMB while looking at a door, leaving it usable for normal operations otherwise. Tell me if it misbehaves.

### Door Modes

- **Everyone** (Default) : Players, Build Camera, Survivors (and Animals if turned on)
- **Players** : Players, Build Camera
- Players &amp; Survivors : same as Everyone, Animals excluded.
- Manual : same as if the mod were off.

Modes are saved per world. When you look at a door inside your base whose mode is not Everyone, its mode shows under the crosshair.

### Secret Doors

Secret doors, shelves, floors and stairs only ever work in your base. Look at one and press **Shift + MMB** (LB + Y) to change its mode. Only the message tells you the mode; there is no label.

- **Close Only** (Default) : never opens by itself, closes once every player has left.
- **Players** : opens and closes for players, like a door.
- **Manual** : same as if the mod were off.

### Opening/Closing by Hand

You can still use any door as usual. A door you open or close by hand **stays that way while you are near it**, then goes back to working on its own once everyone has left.

---

## Settings

Press **Shift + F7** in game (or **Open Settings Window** on the mod's page in Kiln's menu). Every change applies at once; hover a setting to see what it does.

- **Mod Enabled**: the whole mod on or off.
- **Bases Only**: on by default. Turn it off and doors everywhere open and close by themselves. Door modes, their key and the label stay for doors in your base.
- **Bypass Locked Doors**: off by default, so doors that need a lockpick or a key stay shut until you pick or unlock them. Turn it on and they open by themselves too, which unlocks them for good.
- **Players / Survivors / Build Camera / Animals**: who opens doors. Animals are off by default, so your farm stays in.
- **Open Distance** and **Close Distance**: how close someone has to be for a door to open, and how far everyone has to be for it to close, in steps of 0.1 m (hold Shift on the - and + buttons for 0.5 m).
- **Height Reach**: someone on another floor (above or below this distance) neither opens a door nor keeps it open.
- **Close Delay**: seconds a door stays open after everyone has left.
- **Respect Hand Toggles**: the "stays that way while you are near it" rule above.
- **Close Doors Opened By Hand**: off, and only doors the mod opened close by themselves.
- **Door Label**: the mode under the crosshair.
- **Messages**: the on-screen message when you change a door's mode.

---

## Requirements

- [Kiln](https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln) mod loader, **0.2.0-dev.31 or newer**.

## Installation

1. Close the game.
2. Add the archive through Kiln.
3. Start the game and walk up to a door in your base.

If you use the original AutoDoors, turn it off: both would try to move the same doors.

## Compatibility

- **Works in a world you host** (single player or as the host). The mode keys only work for the host. Multiplayer with friends joining and dedicated servers are not tested yet.
